{"ts": 1784343167.308043, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the whole way. Price moved favorably almost immediately (+2 by t=1m) and built a strong trend to +50-56pts by t=15-20m, with several pullbacks (biggest: +56 to +19.5 on a 1m bar low around t=22-23m) that each recovered to stay well above +36pts -- never approached breakeven or negative after the first two minutes, so there was no wrong-direction signal to act on. Fires (HA/PROPP/KMDR) flipped against direction repeatedly during pullbacks but price kept holding a large cushion, confirming these were normal chop/give-back within a working trade, not a breakdown. Next time I'd watch for giveback ratio approaching/exceeding 100% AND price approaching zero/negative simultaneously as the real bail trigger -- neither happened here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 27}
